# AI SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE & INTEGRATION SPECIFICATION (AI.doc)
================================================================================
Document Version: 2.1.0
System Designation: Auto-TG Gameplay Supervisor & Multi-Game Autoplay Platform
Primary Language Stacks: Python 3.10+, Node.js 18+ (CommonJS)
Target Platforms: Telegram WebApps (Catizen, Rignite)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. EXECUTIVE OVERVIEW FOR AI AGENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This repository is an autonomous gameplay supervisor designed to operate 24/7
without human intervention. It coordinates, monitors, and recovers sub-engines
that interact with Telegram mini-apps.

Core Pillars:
1. Process Supervision (`auto_player.py`):
   Spawns child processes (`node play_catizen.js`, `python rignite_tap_engine.py`),
   captures stdout streams non-blockingly, intercepts structured IPC JSON lines,
   and manages process lifecycle (auto-restart with exponential backoff).
2. Live Observability (Aiohttp Web Dashboard on port 8080):
   Serves a single-page reactive dashboard (`WEB_DASHBOARD_HTML`) backed by
   REST endpoints (`/api/status`, `/api/control`).
3. Reporting & Auditing:
   Aggregates periodic metrics (1-hour window), renders rich HTML audit reports
   to Telegraph (`api.graph.org`), and dispatches notifications via Pyrogram
   to Telegram Topics (Chat: `-1003959353966`, Topic 2: Catizen, Topic 4: Rignite).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. COMPONENT MAP & FILE STRUCTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.
├── auto_player.py
│   ├── AutoPlayerSupervisor: Main thread orchestrator.
│   ├── GameTracker: State container, log buffer, and delta math engine.
